-- A rule at the top of a file whose name holds a dot, and a rule of the last
-- name under a section, must not print the same entry (overnight card O6,
-- 2026-10-11; found in review). Both defaults are TYPICALLY: 3 on
-- `Pricing.scaled` at the top, 5 on `scaled` in `§ Pricing`. The rows answer 30,
-- 50 and 80, and list `` `Pricing.scaled` ``, `Pricing.scaled` and both: an
-- owner with no section in front of it is quoted the way L4 writes it in source,
-- so the two are told apart.

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Pricing.scaled` MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
useOne MEANS `Pricing.scaled` WITH base IS n

§ `Pricing`

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 5
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
useTwo MEANS scaled WITH base IS n

§ `Use`

@export default Combine
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      one IS A BOOLEAN
      two IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS (IF one THEN useOne n ELSE 0) PLUS (IF two THEN useTwo n ELSE 0)
